==Trivia==
* Kitsune is the second fan-made [[Blox Fruits|fruit]] to be added to the game, with the first being [[Sound]]. 
** The original concept was created by @Kuzuryu_Kei (X Handle), one of the winners of the first fan fruit/art contest.
* Kitsune is currently the third most expensive fruit in the game behind [[Control]] and [[Dragon]]. 
* Kitsune is the first [[Beast]] fruit that allows allied players to mount, the second being [[Dragon]].
* It is worth noting that [[Agility]] (Rabbit's V3 ability) does not have nearly as much effect as when not transformed. While it is noticeable, it is mostly negligible.
* Despite being based on a nine-tailed fox, Kitsune normally only has three tails and five tails when transformed; this is probably due to the design of the model, although it still has nine tails in the icon.
** The same happens to Inventory Icon and Physical Fruit, while the Inventory Icon model has 4 tails, Physical Fruit only has 3 tails.
* When ''walking'' whilst using Kitsune with two or more tails, the player animation will shift from crawling on all fours to an upright & skipping animation.
* Kitsune used to have a move called "Tailed Beast Bomb" as its [C] move, which got changed into "Fox Fire Disruption" and the [F] move, "'''Wild''' Assault" , was called "'''Swift''' Assault" in the fruit's sneak peek. 
* All of Kitsune's moves (excluding {{Ability|V}}) can only be held for 12 seconds.
* In the fan made design, the [X] move was called "'''Claws''' of Burning Agony" which was changed to "'''Tails''' of Burning Agony" in the game.
* A physical Kitsune Fruit can also be obtained at a very low chance (0.1%/1 in 1000) by offering [[Azure Ember]]s to the [[Kitsune Shrine]] in the [[Third Sea]].
* The player can reach up to 9.3x of their original speed by using Kitsune's 2 tails (+100%/2x speed), having [[Rabbit|Rabbit's]] race v2 passive (+100%/2x speed), [[Rabbit]] [[Agility|race's V3 ability]] (+400%/4x speed) and [[Pilot Helmet|Pilot Helmet]] (+130%/1.3x speed).
* Kitsune is the second fruit with a mutation, the first being [[Tiger]].
* Although Kitsune and reworked [[Control]] share the robux price of ({{Robux|4,000}}), they do not share the same {{Money|Money}} value. Kitsune is valued at {{Money|8,000,000}} and [[Control]] is valued at {{Money|9,000,000}}.


